---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

// TODO(owner): set the real date when the reviewed policy goes live, and remove
// the review banner below once an Australian solicitor has signed this off.
const lastUpdated = '26 September 2026';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MSRM collects, uses, stores and protects personal information, in line with the Australian Privacy Principles."
>
  <section class="container-x py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="h2 mt-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-mute mt-3 text-sm">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <!-- TEMPLATE BANNER — remove after legal review -->
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">
      <strong>Template — review by an Australian solicitor before launch.</strong>
      This policy is a professionally structured template, not legal advice. Have it
      reviewed and adapted to your circumstances before relying on it.
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">1. Who we are</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our") provides a restaurant management platform —
          point of sale, kitchen display, inventory, online ordering and accounting —
          to hospitality businesses in Australia, together with this marketing website.
          We are committed to handling personal information in accordance with the
          <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This policy covers personal information we collect through this website and in
          the course of providing the {SITE.name} platform. Data our restaurant customers
          enter about <em>their</em> own customers and staff inside the platform is
          processed on their behalf and is governed primarily by our agreement with them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">2. What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong>Enquiry and demo details</strong> — when you request a demo or contact us: your name, email address, phone number, restaurant or business name, and anything you include in your message.</li>
          <li><strong>Account details</strong> — if you sign up for the platform: your name, email, phone number, business details (including ABN), and billing information.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — pages visited, approximate location (city level), device and browser type, and referral source, collected via analytics cookies (see section 7).</li>
          <li><strong>Support communications</strong> — records of emails, calls and support requests.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We do not knowingly collect sensitive information (as defined in the Privacy Act)
          through this website, and we ask that you do not submit it via our forms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">3. How we use your information</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>To respond to your enquiry and arrange product demonstrations;</li>
          <li>To provide, operate, support and improve the {SITE.name} platform;</li>
          <li>To process billing and account administration;</li>
          <li>To send service updates and, with your consent, marketing communications (every marketing email includes an unsubscribe link);</li>
          <li>To understand how the website is used so we can improve it;</li>
          <li>To comply with our legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">4. Disclosure to third parties</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">We do not sell personal information. We disclose it only to service providers who help us run the business, and only for the purposes above:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure</strong> — our website and platform are hosted with cloud providers (currently Vercel and Render);</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — Google Analytics, where enabled (see section 7);</li>
          <li><strong>Communications and CRM tools</strong> — used to manage enquiries and support;</li>
          <li><strong>Payment processors</strong> — for subscription billing (we do not store full card numbers ourselves);</li>
          <li><strong>Professional advisers and authorities</strong> — where required or authorised by law.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">5. Overseas disclosure</h2>
        {/*
          OWNER — APP 8 disclosure. The paragraph below is written for the CURRENT
          state (data at rest still hosted overseas). It is accurate today. Do NOT
          claim Australian hosting until the AU data-residency cutover is complete
          (backend/docs/AU_DATA_RESIDENCY.md). AFTER cutover, replace the paragraph
          with this post-cutover version:

          "Our application database, file storage and backups are hosted in Australia.
          Certain processing occurs overseas — our application compute is served from
          Singapore, and our analytics (Google) and marketing-site edge (Vercel)
          providers operate infrastructure in other regions. Where personal information
          is disclosed overseas, we take reasonable steps to ensure the recipient
          handles it consistently with the APPs, as required by APP 8."
        */}
        <p class="mt-2">
          Some of our service providers store or process data outside Australia — in
          particular, our cloud hosting and analytics providers operate infrastructure in
          the <strong>United States</strong> and other regions. Where personal information
          is disclosed overseas, we take reasonable steps to ensure the recipient handles
          it consistently with the APPs, as required by APP 8.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">6. Storage, security and retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse,
          interference, loss, and unauthorised access, modification or disclosure —
          including encryption in transit (HTTPS/TLS), access controls, and hosting with
          reputable providers. No internet transmission is completely secure, so we cannot
          guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes above or as
          required by law (for example, tax and accounting records), after which we take
          reasonable steps to destroy or de-identify it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This website uses Google Analytics 4 to understand aggregate visitor behaviour.
          Analytics runs only when enabled for the environment; no analytics cookies are
          set otherwise. You can opt out of Google Analytics across all websites using
          Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-700 underline">browser opt-out add-on</a>,
          or limit cookies through your browser settings. The site remains fully usable
          without analytics cookies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">8. Access and correction</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You may request access to the personal information we hold about you, and ask us
          to correct it if it is inaccurate, out of date, incomplete or misleading. Email
          us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-brand-700 underline">{SITE.email}</a> —
          we will respond within a reasonable period (usually 30 days). We may need to
          verify your identity before giving access, and in limited cases permitted by the
          Privacy Act we may refuse access, in which case we will tell you why.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">9. Complaints</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If you believe we have mishandled your personal information, please contact us
          first at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-brand-700 underline">{SITE.email}</a>
          and we will investigate and respond within a reasonable period. If you are not
          satisfied with our response, you may complain to the Office of the Australian
          Information Commissioner (OAIC) at
          <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-700 underline">oaic.gov.au</a>
          or by calling 1300 363 992.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">10. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may update this policy from time to time. The current version will always be
          published on this page with its "Last updated" date. Material changes affecting
          platform customers will be notified by email.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">11. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Privacy questions and requests:
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-brand-700 underline">{SITE.email}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm"><a href="/" class="text-brand-700 underline">← Back home</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>
